    contactinfo: fix the key so CQ zone actually reaches the packet
    
    send_contact_info()'s ADD path set contact_info["zn"] -- not a key the
    contact_info template has, so dicttoxml just serialized it as a second,
    unused <zn> tag nobody reads. The real "zone" key that actually becomes
    the packet's <zone> element was never touched, so it stayed frozen at
    its class-level default ("5") for every single QSO logged this way.
    
    logwindow.py's two send_contactreplace() call sites already had this
    right (contact_info["zone"] = ...); the ADD path just used the wrong
    name. One-character fix: "zn" -> "zone".
    
    Downstream effect: a consumer that groups QSOs by worked-station CQ zone
    (e.g. a "zones worked" panel) saw every QSO as zone 5 regardless of who
