    Add ft8_handler to CWT, SST, MST and CW Open plugins
    
    The UDP ADIF listener on :9876 parsed incoming records and then dropped
    them for these four CW sprints, because the plugins had no ft8_handler
    for __main__ to dispatch to. An external CW logger can now log QSOs into
    CWT, K1USN SST, ICWC MST and CWOPS Open.
    
    Each handler follows the arrl_field_day model: it fills the plugin's own
    exchange widgets and contact fields, then calls save_contact(), which
    runs the plugin's set_contact_vars() and points(), writes the record and
    refreshes the log, check, statistics and rate windows.
    
    ADIF field mapping:
    
      CWT       NAME -> other_1/Name, SRX_STRING or SRX -> other_2, and
                NR is stored as "name number". SentNr keeps coming from the
                contest's SentExchange setting.
      K1USN SST NAME -> other_1/Name, STATE or SRX_STRING -> other_2/Sect,
                defaulting to DX when neither is present.
      ICWC MST  NAME plus SRX_STRING or SRX -> other_2, which
                set_contact_vars() splits into Name and NR; STX -> other_1
                and SentNr. A logger that puts the whole received exchange
                into SRX_STRING is handled too.
      CW Open   SRX -> NR, NAME -> Name, joined as "number name" for
                other_2; STX -> other_1 and SentNr.
    
    All four also set Call, Mode, Freq, QSXFreq and Band from the packet.

